Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-glymur: Do not park mdss_mdp_clk_src

clk_rcg2_shared_ops parks the RCG on XO when it is registered. For the
MDP clock that stops the display engine that is still scanning out the
firmware framebuffer, so efifb/simpledrm go black as soon as
dispcc-glymur probes. With defconfig that driver is a module, so this
happens in stage 2, right after the root filesystem is mounted.

dispcc-x1e80100, -sc8280xp and -sm8450 already use
clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops for disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src for this
reason; do the same on Glymur (and therefore Mahua).

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
index 32cc5226b..153601bb5 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
@@ -623,7 +623,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src = {
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_7,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_7),
 		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops,
 	},
 };
 
